      "math_academy_id": "e-8431",
      "problem": "Given that $X$ is a random variable such that $X\\sim U[-9,-3],$ find $\\textrm{SD}[X].$ Round your answer to three decimal places.",
      "worked_solution": "If the random variable $X$ is distributed uniformly over the interval $[a,b],$ then \n\n$$\n\\textrm{Var}[X] = \\dfrac{(b-a)^2}{12}.\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have $a=-9$ and $b=-3.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\textrm{Var}[X] = \\dfrac{(-3-(-9))^2}{12} = \\dfrac{36}{12} = 3.\n$$\n\nFinally,\n\n$$\n\\textrm{SD}[X] = \\sqrt{3} \\approx 1.732.\n$$",
